($x_0$ is omitted).
$a,b,c,d$ are complex constants
and $(A,B,C,g_2,g_3,k)$ algebraic expressions of $(a,b,c,d)$.
When the degree of $P$ in (\ref{eqBinomial}) is maximal (i.e.~$2 n$),
anyone of the factors of $P$ can be set to $1$ by a homography.
An equivalent table (however without the solutions) can be found
in Garnier \cite[p 127 Table (T)]{Garnier1960}.
